{"attributes":{"stable_path":"/documentation/Documentation@234853ac-3779-4026-aeb1-e9f58f624b2d","sysml_id":"234853ac-3779-4026-aeb1-e9f58f624b2d","element_id":"234853ac-3779-4026-aeb1-e9f58f624b2d","sysml_type":"Documentation","owner_id":"cb5ec657-8d66-44a2-a497-23b071f651a6","owning_namespace_id":"cb5ec657-8d66-44a2-a497-23b071f651a6","owning_relationship_id":"90fe0951-e1d5-470c-b953-5bc5f7f9fc3b","owning_membership_id":"90fe0951-e1d5-470c-b953-5bc5f7f9fc3b","is_library_element":false,"is_implied_included":false,"body":"Perception compute unit (processor + memory). Fuses the camera,\nLiDAR, and infrared inputs and runs the detection/classification\npipeline, producing the TigerDetection result. A random hardware\nfault here corrupts or halts the detection pipeline.\nRequirements: TDS_SEN_004, TDS_ALG_001, TDS_ALG_002, TDS_ALG_003,\nTDS_ALG_004.\n"},"concept":"documentation","metamodel":"SysMLv2","namespace":"System_Model_Tiger_Detection"},
{"attributes":{"stable_path":"/documentation/Documentation@237dfc37-970f-42fc-bd86-ecdd39a498ad","sysml_id":"237dfc37-970f-42fc-bd86-ecdd39a498ad","element_id":"237dfc37-970f-42fc-bd86-ecdd39a498ad","sysml_type":"Documentation","owner_id":"918d1a9d-9146-4fb5-9681-ee92255374e3","owning_namespace_id":"918d1a9d-9146-4fb5-9681-ee92255374e3","owning_relationship_id":"3d46ee28-e36a-4e72-81d0-66cd2a8d9484","owning_membership_id":"3d46ee28-e36a-4e72-81d0-66cd2a8d9484","is_library_element":false,"is_implied_included":false,"body":"Architecture model for the Tiger Detection System (initial baseline).\nThis model reflects only the initial system requirements in\n../1-sys-req/requirements/tigerDetectionReq.rst: detect a tiger and warn\nthe operator, with start/stop control. The safe-state, sensor-degradation\nand operating-condition-monitoring functions are NOT modelled here — they\nare improvements raised as tasks by the system-level safety analysis and\nwill be added once the requirements are updated. Documentation items below\ncite the corresponding Sphinx-Needs TDS_* IDs; use those IDs to navigate\nthe rendered requirements rather than duplicating requirement text here.\n"},"concept":"documentation","metamodel":"SysMLv2","namespace":"System_Model_Tiger_Detection"},
